IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ma-misrepresentation`

-- Misrepresentation Act 1967, ss 1-4 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_misrepresentation-act-1967.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `s 1`

#ASSERT `the representee is entitled to rescind under section 1` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the representee is entitled to rescind under section 1` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the representee is entitled to rescind under section 1` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the representee is entitled to rescind under section 1` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the representee is entitled to rescind under section 1` FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `s 2(1)`

`a seller's false statement, no defence` MEANS Claim WITH
    `the representee entered the contract after the misrepresentation` IS TRUE
    `the misrepresentation was made by another party to the contract` IS TRUE
    `the representee suffered loss as a result` IS TRUE
    `the representor would be liable in damages had it been fraudulent` IS TRUE
    `the representor proved reasonable ground to believe the facts true` IS FALSE
    `the representor proved actual belief up to the time of contracting` IS FALSE

`a seller with reasonable ground but no proof of belief` MEANS Claim WITH
    `the representee entered the contract after the misrepresentation` IS TRUE
    `the misrepresentation was made by another party to the contract` IS TRUE
    `the representee suffered loss as a result` IS TRUE
    `the representor would be liable in damages had it been fraudulent` IS TRUE
    `the representor proved reasonable ground to believe the facts true` IS TRUE
    `the representor proved actual belief up to the time of contracting` IS FALSE

`a seller who believed it but had no reasonable ground` MEANS Claim WITH
    `the representee entered the contract after the misrepresentation` IS TRUE
    `the misrepresentation was made by another party to the contract` IS TRUE
    `the representee suffered loss as a result` IS TRUE
    `the representor would be liable in damages had it been fraudulent` IS TRUE
    `the representor proved reasonable ground to believe the facts true` IS FALSE
    `the representor proved actual belief up to the time of contracting` IS TRUE

`a seller who proved ground and belief` MEANS Claim WITH
    `the representee entered the contract after the misrepresentation` IS TRUE
    `the misrepresentation was made by another party to the contract` IS TRUE
    `the representee suffered loss as a result` IS TRUE
    `the representor would be liable in damages had it been fraudulent` IS TRUE
    `the representor proved reasonable ground to believe the facts true` IS TRUE
    `the representor proved actual belief up to the time of contracting` IS TRUE

`a statement by a stranger to the contract` MEANS Claim WITH
    `the representee entered the contract after the misrepresentation` IS TRUE
    `the misrepresentation was made by another party to the contract` IS FALSE
    `the representee suffered loss as a result` IS TRUE
    `the representor would be liable in damages had it been fraudulent` IS TRUE
    `the representor proved reasonable ground to believe the facts true` IS FALSE
    `the representor proved actual belief up to the time of contracting` IS FALSE

`a false statement causing no loss` MEANS Claim WITH
    `the representee entered the contract after the misrepresentation` IS TRUE
    `the misrepresentation was made by another party to the contract` IS TRUE
    `the representee suffered loss as a result` IS FALSE
    `the representor would be liable in damages had it been fraudulent` IS TRUE
    `the representor proved reasonable ground to believe the facts true` IS FALSE
    `the representor proved actual belief up to the time of contracting` IS FALSE

`a statement not actionable even if fraudulent` MEANS Claim WITH
    `the representee entered the contract after the misrepresentation` IS TRUE
    `the misrepresentation was made by another party to the contract` IS TRUE
    `the representee suffered loss as a result` IS TRUE
    `the representor would be liable in damages had it been fraudulent` IS FALSE
    `the representor proved reasonable ground to believe the facts true` IS FALSE
    `the representor proved actual belief up to the time of contracting` IS FALSE

`a statement made after the contract` MEANS Claim WITH
    `the representee entered the contract after the misrepresentation` IS FALSE
    `the misrepresentation was made by another party to the contract` IS TRUE
    `the representee suffered loss as a result` IS TRUE
    `the representor would be liable in damages had it been fraudulent` IS TRUE
    `the representor proved reasonable ground to believe the facts true` IS FALSE
    `the representor proved actual belief up to the time of contracting` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the representor is liable in damages under section 2(1)` `a seller's false statement, no defence`
#ASSERT `the representor is liable in damages under section 2(1)` `a seller with reasonable ground but no proof of belief`
#ASSERT `the representor is liable in damages under section 2(1)` `a seller who believed it but had no reasonable ground`
#ASSERT NOT `the representor is liable in damages under section 2(1)` `a seller who proved ground and belief`
#ASSERT NOT `the representor is liable in damages under section 2(1)` `a statement by a stranger to the contract`
#ASSERT NOT `the representor is liable in damages under section 2(1)` `a false statement causing no loss`
#ASSERT NOT `the representor is liable in damages under section 2(1)` `a statement not actionable even if fraudulent`
#ASSERT NOT `the representor is liable in damages under section 2(1)` `a statement made after the contract`

#ASSERT `the representor proved the section 2(1) defence` `a seller who proved ground and belief`
#ASSERT NOT `the representor proved the section 2(1) defence` `a seller with reasonable ground but no proof of belief`

